{
  "id": "tah-trig",
  "chapterNumber": "4",
  "title": {
    "en": "Trigonometry",
    "ar": null
  },
  "railLabel": {
    "en": "Trigonometry",
    "ar": "المثلثات"
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Ratios of the special angles, the unit circle, the Pythagorean identity, and the behaviour of the sine and cosine graphs.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Trig essentials",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( \\sin30^{\\circ}=\\tfrac12,\\ \\cos60^{\\circ}=\\tfrac12,\\ \\tan45^{\\circ}=1 \\). The identity \\( \\sin^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{2}\\theta=1 \\) holds for all \\( \\theta \\). Convert with \\( 180^{\\circ}=\\pi \\) radians. The graphs of \\( \\sin \\) and \\( \\cos \\) have period \\( 2\\pi \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Change the amplitude and frequency of \\( y=A\\sin(Bx) \\). The amber lines mark \\( \\pm A \\); the period is \\( \\tfrac{2\\pi}{B} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The sine wave",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "tahWaveCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "The graph of y equals A sine B x with adjustable amplitude and frequency",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "tahWaveDataBtn",
          "panelId": "tahWaveDataPanel",
          "descId": "tahWaveDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "tahWaveDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points along the current sine wave",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "tahAmp",
            "valueDisplayId": "tahAmpV",
            "label": {
              "en": "Amplitude <b>A =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Amplitude A",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 1,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 2,
            "step": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "tahFreq",
            "valueDisplayId": "tahFreqV",
            "label": {
              "en": "Frequency <b>B =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Frequency B",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 1,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 1
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "tahWAmp",
            "label": {
              "en": "amplitude",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber"
          },
          {
            "id": "tahWPeriod",
            "label": {
              "en": "period",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Larger \\( A \\) stretches the wave taller; larger \\( B \\) packs more cycles into the same width.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Special angles",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sin30^{\\circ}=\\tfrac12 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Identity",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sin^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{2}\\theta=1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Radians",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 180^{\\circ}=\\pi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Period",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sin,\\cos:\\ 2\\pi \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Convert \\( 180^{\\circ} \\) to radians. \\[ \\pi. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A right triangle has opposite side \\( 3 \\) and hypotenuse \\( 6 \\). Find \\( \\theta \\). \\( \\sin\\theta=\\tfrac36=\\tfrac12 \\): \\[ \\theta=30^{\\circ}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Given \\(\\sin\\theta=\\frac{3}{5}\\) and \\(\\theta\\) is in the first quadrant, find \\(\\cos\\theta\\), \\(\\tan\\theta\\), and \\(\\sin(2\\theta).\\) <details><summary>Show solution</summary><div>\\(\\cos\\theta=\\frac{4}{5}\\) (Pythagorean identity: \\(\\cos^2\\theta=1-\\frac{9}{25}=\\frac{16}{25}\\)). \\(\\tan\\theta=\\frac{3/5}{4/5}=\\frac{3}{4}.\\) \\(\\sin(2\\theta)=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=2\\cdot\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot\\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{24}{25}.\\)</div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
